			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Gnomeregan was the city of the {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link}, a wonder of the world built into the western hills of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}. Its halls were full of great engines, clockwork servants and devices that no other people could have dreamed of. Today it is a poisoned ruin. Its gates are watched by the sick and maddened survivors of its fall, its depths crawl with {link:troggs}troggs{/link} and living slime, and at its heart sits the gnome who betrayed it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The gnomes built Gnomeregan with their own hands, as neighbors and friends of the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. No chronicle records the year of its founding. For generations it was the seat of the High Tinker and the pride of the gnomish people, and from its workshops came many of the machines that served the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Fall",
			text = [=[The troggs came up from the depths beneath the city in numbers the gnomes could not hold back. High Tinker {link:gelbin-mekkatorque}Gelbin Mekkatorque{/link} chose to purge them with a weapon of the gnomes' own making. It killed troggs, but it killed a great many gnomes as well, and it left the city drenched in poison. Many who lived were changed into lepers, sick in body and empty in mind. The rest fled to {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. Behind them, {link:mekgineer-thermaplugg}Mekgineer Thermaplugg{/link}, whom the High Tinker had trusted, took the city for himself.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Walls",
			text = [=[• {b}The entrance.{/b} A {link:gnomes}gnome{/link} named Emi Shortfuse holds the gates against the troggs with explosives and very little patience.
